An element's start tag is hidden, so its tag name and the attribute that names it among its siblings (`name`,
`id` or `key`, in any namespace: `android:name`, `android:id`) are `key` fields of the element itself, as an
object element's key is in other grammars. The diff matcher pairs `<string name="app_name">` with its
counterpart by `string name="app_name"`, `<activity android:name=".Main">` by its android:name, a storyboard's
`<view key="view" id="...">` by its key and id, and a lone `<application>` by its tag: a member's key is its
name within its scope (packages/syntechs/src/diff/matcher.ts, memberName). Upstream's STag, ETag and
EmptyElemTag nodes are gone; nvim-treesitter's tag patterns read the names from the element instead.

Character data is its text without the spaces around it, and those spaces are an _S in the content, as
whitespace between tags is in tree-sitter-html: upstream's CharData took every run between tags, so each
indented line held a whitespace node that an inserted element or a reindent changed. scanner.c's change is
ported in src/grammars/xml/scanner.ts.

An attribute value's text is `string_content` nodes, as JSON's is: upstream reads it a character at a time,
in hidden tokens, so an edit inside `"@string/app_name"` fell in no leaf and the diff could not mark what
changed.

